{
  "version": 1,
  "about": [
    "The catalogue behind the scan archive's PLANNER tab: which station kits, extractors and gear exist, and what each costs to make.",
    "cost is null until it has been entered: the planner then lists the item as 'cost not entered' instead of treating it as free. A cost is an object of resource id -> amount, e.g. {\"metal\": 500, \"microchips\": 20}; an empty object {} means genuinely free. 'manhours' and 'credits' are resources like any other. For something bought from an AI station the cost IS the buy price in credits.",
    "Gear can be made two ways. With upgrade_from it is an upgrade: its blueprint is run on upgrade_qty of the item named, which is used up, and cost is that ONE step; the planner adds up the whole chain (a Mk III = its own step + the Mk II step + the bought Mk I). With a blueprint but no upgrade_from it is built from scratch and cost is everything it takes. With neither it is bought and cost is its price.",
    "Blueprints are reusable (Uses: infinity), so they are never counted as used up. blueprint_price, when known, is what buying that blueprint costs once; the planner can add it to the totals if you tick the option.",
    "per_day is how much of the resource ONE extractor produces per day (the 'Production' line on its item tooltip: promethium 1,440 = 1 per 60 s; the rare resources copper/gold/titanium/oil 8.64 = 1 per 10,000 s; wood cutter 8,640; advanced 17,280; industrial 25,920 = 3 per 10 s). per_day_inferred: true marks a rate assumed rather than read off an item: the basic metal drill, silicon drill and harvester are assumed to be 8,640, the figure the basic wood cutter shows (the basic : advanced : industrial ladder is 1 : 2 : 3 for every resource seen).",
    "tech / size are what the item shows in an AI station's shop or a captured station's item stats (Tech = the tier players call 't9'). null = not seen yet.",
    "kind says where a kit goes: planet (attached to a planet, up to 3 per planet), moon (1 per moon), unattached (free-standing in a system: no extractors, used for defence). station_slots is the character station-slot budget one station uses: 9 for a planet-side kit (colony_tool station_slot_cost) and for an unattached kit (the player: same as attached), 2 for the lunar kit. It is null where not supplied; the planner then says so rather than counting it as 0.",
    "Sources (2026-10-12): the player's screenshots of the AI station's shop ('Station' tab: station kits and extractors; gear tab: Mk I gear; blueprints tab: Layered Plating) and of the blueprints' item tooltips (upgrade and Layered Plating costs). Mk II = T6 and Mk III = T9 per the player. The Mk II names are known from the client; the sensor Mk II, every Mk III key and attached_station_kit_ii are inferred from the same naming pattern (the labels are exact). The Dominion Station and the (Small) Central Commands are not in the planner.",
    "Only the keys and items listed here appear in the planner. To add an item or a tier, add an entry; nothing else needs to change."
  ],
